dot-cat(1) -- Dump the contents of dotfile(s) to stdout
=======================================================

## SYNOPSIS

`dot cat` [-h] <file>...

## DESCRIPTION

Dump the contents of the dotfile(s) to stdout, emulating the functionality of `cat`.

Part of dot(1).

## OPTIONS

  * `-h`, `--h`:
    Show command help.

  * <file>:
    One or more managed files. Paths are relative to the dotfile repo.
